#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:2
msgid "Usage without poetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:4
msgid ""
"Poe the Poet was originally intended as the missing task runner for |"
"poetry_link|. But it also works great with |uv_link|, or any other kind of "
"virtualenv, or as a general purpose task runner! This behaviour is "
"configurable via the :ref:`tool.poe.executor global option<Configure the "
"executor for a task>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:84
msgid "<a href=\"https://python-poetry.org/\" target=\"_blank\">poetry</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:80
msgid "<a href=\"https://docs.astral.sh/uv/\" target=\"_blank\">uv</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:6
msgid ""
"By default poe will run tasks in your project's virtual environment. Poe "
"will deduce what kind of project is present by detecting tool specific "
"tables in ``pyproject.toml`` such as :toml:`tool.poetry`, lock files such as "
"``uv.lock``, or a virtualenv at ``./.venv`` or ``./venv`` relative to the "
"``pyproject.toml``. If no virtualenv is found then poe will run tasks "
"without any special environment management."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:8
msgid ""
"Poe the Poet can also be used as a :doc:`global task runner<./"
"global_tasks>`, scoped to your system rather than any particular project, "
"like shell aliases by sweeter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:12
msgid "Usage with uv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:14
msgid ""
"|uv_link| is another popular tool for managing project dependencies with a "
"``pyproject.toml`` file. If the ``pyproject.toml`` contains a ``[tool.uv]`` "
"table, or the project directory contains a ``uv.lock`` files then Poe the "
"Poet will recognise this and activate the UvExecutor to execute tasks using "
"``uv run``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:16
msgid ""
"In case your uv project doesn't have a lockfile or any uv specific config, "
"you can still force poe to use the uv executor like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:18
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"executor.type = \"uv\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:23
msgid "So Poe the Poet also works well with uv."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:27
msgid "Usage without pyproject.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:29
msgid ""
"When using Poe the Poet outside of a poetry (or other |pep518_link|) "
"project, you can avoid the potential confusion of creating a ``pyproject."
"toml`` file and instead name the file ``poe_tasks.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:88
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0518/\" target=\"_blank\">PEP 518</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:33
msgid "Usage with with json or yaml instead of toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:35
msgid ""
"As an alternative to toml, poethepoet configuration can also be provided via "
"yaml or json files. When searching for a tasks file to load within a certain "
"directory poe will try the following file names in order:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:37
msgid "pyproject.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:38
msgid "poe_tasks.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:39 ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:46
#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:62
msgid "poe_tasks.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:40
msgid "poe_tasks.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:42
msgid ""
"If ``pyproject.toml`` exists but does not contain the key prefix ``tool."
"poe`` then the search continues with `poe_tasks.toml`. If one of the listed "
"``poe_tasks.*`` files exist then the search is terminated, even if the file "
"is empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:44
msgid ""
"When config is loaded from a file other than ``pyproject.toml`` the ``tool."
"poe`` namespace for poe config is optional. So for example the following two "
"``poe_tasks.yaml`` files are equivalent and both valid:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:46
msgid ""
"env:\n"
"  VAR0: FOO\n"
"\n"
"tasks:\n"
"  show-vars:\n"
"    cmd: \"echo $VAR0 $VAR1 $VAR2\"\n"
"    env:\n"
"      VAR1: BAR\n"
"    args:\n"
"      - name: VAR2\n"
"        options: [\"--var\"]\n"
"        default: BAZ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/without_poetry.rst:62
msgid ""
"tool:\n"
"  poe:\n"
"    env:\n"
"      VAR0: FOO\n"
"\n"
"    tasks:\n"
"      show-vars:\n"
"        cmd: \"echo $VAR0 $VAR1 $VAR2\"\n"
"        env:\n"
"          VAR1: BAR\n"
"        args:\n"
"          - name: VAR2\n"
"            options: [\"--var\"]\n"
"            default: BAZ"
msgstr ""
